dc: a present without a release fence returns only once its frame is on screen

TrimUI's Vulkan driver (libVK_IMG, VK_KHR_display, always two swapchain images) passes no
release fence and takes the return of DCDisplayContextConfigure as the sign that its other
image has left the screen. The call returned as soon as the configuration was queued, right
after the previous flip, while that image stayed on screen until the next one; the next frame
was drawn into it, so the top rows showed a frame two presents older than the rows below (seen
on the TrimUI Brick in dispcap captures of the display engine's output).
Configurations without a release fence now return once their frame is on screen, i.e. once
every earlier configuration has retired (the display driver retires one when the display has
taken the next), at most 100 ms. The GL window system passes a release fence and waits on it;
it is unchanged. /sys/module/pvrsrvkm/parameters/dc_present_waits_for_flip (default Y) turns
the wait off for measurements; /sys/kernel/debug/pvr/gpu00/debug_dump shows how long the
presents of each running program waited. 2026-10-23.

